# okf-sdk configuration for commands run from the repo root
# (`scripts/dev.sh`, `uv run okf-mcp`, `uv run okf-web`). Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and edit.
# Real paths and credentials belong in `.env`, never in this file.
#
# `.env` is read from the directory the command starts in, so a server
# launched from elsewhere needs its own copy or real environment variables.

# OKF_HOME is NOT read from `.env`: export it in the shell instead.
# Workspaces live in <OKF_HOME>/workspaces/<name>; the default home is ~/.okf.
#   export OKF_HOME=/path/to/okf-home

# Default target for okf-mcp. Tool args and X-OKF-Workspace / X-OKF-Bundle
# headers override these; when unset, the session's earlier pick, the only
# candidate, or the user (elicitation) decides.
# OKF_WORKSPACE=team
# OKF_BUNDLE=notes

# Semantic search (okf-mcp `search` tool and the okf-web search box): an
# OpenAI-compatible embeddings server, base URL including any /v1 prefix.
# Leave URL and MODEL unset to disable search.
# OKF_EMBEDDING_URL=http://localhost:1234/v1
# OKF_EMBEDDING_MODEL=text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1
# OKF_EMBEDDING_API_KEY=

# Characters of each `_index.md` sent to the embedding model (default 6000).
# Match it to the model's context window: text past the window is silently
# ignored. mxbai-embed-large-v1 (512 tokens) reads about 2000 characters;
# nomic-embed-text-v1.5 handles the default.
# OKF_EMBEDDING_MAX_CHARS=2000

# Ports for `scripts/dev.sh` (a value exported in the shell wins). Unset, the
# script uses 47800 / 47801 / 47802 and moves past any that are busy; a port
# set here is used as is, and the script stops if it is taken.
# MCP_PORT=47800    # okf-mcp, streamable-http at /mcp
# BE_PORT=47801     # okf-web API (also serves the built UI)
# WEB_PORT=47802    # frontend dev server, only with --dev
